# Trivy suppressions — risk-accepted dependency CVEs.
#
# These are the SAME acceptances pip-audit.yml already encodes via
# --ignore-vuln and SECURITY.md documents in full ("Accepted Dependency
# Risks"). Trivy was the only dependency scanner in the fleet without them, so
# every fs and image scan re-raised an alert the threat model had already
# dispositioned -- the reliable way to train an operator to ignore the
# Security tab entirely, which costs more than the finding it surfaces.
#
# Adding an entry here is a security decision, not housekeeping: it needs the
# matching SECURITY.md rationale and a review date, exactly as below.

# chromadb 1.5.9 — pre-auth RCE in Chroma SERVER mode (`chroma run` /
# HttpClient). CyClaw uses the embedded PersistentClient exclusively, in
# process, with no network listener, so the vulnerable path is unreachable in
# this deployment. Any change introducing chromadb.HttpClient or a standalone
# Chroma server re-opens this assessment.
# Review: next chromadb release or 2026-10-01, whichever comes first.
CVE-2026-45829

# nltk 3.9.4 — no fixed release available. nltk (punkt) runs only at corpus
# INDEX time over local, operator-supplied .md/.txt files; no untrusted remote
# input reaches the tokenizer in normal operation.
# Review: next nltk release or 2026-10-01, whichever comes first.
CVE-2026-12243
PYSEC-2026-597
